 "notes": "Constraint from Solar Maximum Mission (SMM) observations of SN1987A using gamma-ray non-detection. The limit accounts for axion production in the proto-neutron star (PNS) from Primakoff and nucleon-nucleon processes, and subsequent axion-to-photon conversion in the stellar magnetic field of the progenitor and the Galactic magnetic field. Data extracted from Figure 1 of the paper. The 95% confidence upper limit covers the axion mass range from ~10^-12 eV to ~0.1 eV. The paper uses SN1987A simulations (SFHo-18.6) with updated Galactic magnetic field models. Physical mass range: 10^-12 to 10^-1 eV.",
